   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "Noted: for this project, notes live in `notes.json` under `NOTES_HOME`. I have no persistent memory tool here, and the project has no `CLAUDE.md`. That means I haven't saved it anywhere, so I can add it to a `CLAUDE.md` if you want it to carry over to later sessions.\n\nFor an empty store, `list` prints nothing and exits with code 0:\n\n```\n$ NOTES_HOME=<empty temp dir> python -m fieldnotes.cli list\n$ echo $?\n0\n```\n\n- **Why it's empty:** `store.load()` returns `[]` when `notes.json` doesn't exist, so the loop in `fieldnotes/cli.py:21` has nothing to print. There's no \"no notes\" message.\n- **`NOTES_HOME` was unset:** In this shell it was empty, and `store.notes_path()` reads `os.environ[\"NOTES_HOME\"]` directly. Running `list` without it set raises a `KeyError`. I ran the command against a fresh temporary directory instead.",
